# L3 e2e — NEGATIVE CONTROL (run via --compare with the other e2e).
# Intent was a self-contradiction trap: at a HIGH starting CO2, would a naive ReAct parrot the
# corpus ops-note magnitude ("lowers CO2 by 150-300 ppm") into a body that contradicts its own
# target and get rejected by the CriticAgent? MEASURED (2026-05-31, --n5): it does NOT — the
# deepseek-v4-flash baseline sets a coherent target (e.g. 800/30min) and a grounded diagnosis with
# no drop-magnitude restatement, so BOTH arms tie at 1.00 (DEVLOG P-011). These tasks are kept as
# a negative control: they document that a STRONG base model handles simple single-anomaly
# incidents naively, which is exactly WHY architecture discrimination has to come from memory
# (the +1.00 ablation) and from misleading-retrieval / multi-step tasks that need the real PDF
# corpus + actuator-coupled simulator (Phase 5) — not from harder single-shot framing on a strong
# base. arm_value() arms the simulator to each task's exact value so the baseline reads what it's told.
